130	### The Maze logo
131	
132	Maze draws the xscreensaver logo inside its maze. The logo data in
133	`logo-50_png.h` is `utils/images/logo-50.gif` from xscreensaver 6.16,
134	re-encoded as 50 by 50 RGB565 pixels and a transparency mask, without
135	changing the design. It is not part of the MIT-licensed code in this
136	repository.
137	
138	The GIF has no licence text of its own. The C file that uses it,
139	`utils/logo.c`, credits the design to Angela Goodman, carries jwz's
140	permission notice (above) for its code, and asks that the logo not be
141	altered: "The logo is xscreensaver's identity". To use a different picture
142	in a local build without committing it, set `XS_LOGO` to the image file (see
143	`AGENTS.md`). The blob format is in `ximage-loader.h`.

